  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PEID, Facilitet f&#xf6;r milj&#xf6;infrastrukturprojekt</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PEID, Priority Environmental Infrastructure for Development - Priority Environmental Infrastructure for Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PEID (Priority&#xa0;Environmental Infrastructure for Development)&#xa0;project aims&#xa0;to develop Serbia&apos;s investment pipeline for environmental infrastructure projects (solid waste and waste water) to the point of financing by providing technical assistance. Special focus is given to waste water investment preparations in the City of Nis and the City of Cacak. PEID support will strengthen Serbia in achieving the EU standards for waste water treatment. The project is implemented by a procured consultant, EPTISA, in cooperation with the Ministry of Environmental Protection in Serbia, and the Department for Project&#xa0;Management (DPM).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Milj&#xf6;infrastrukturprojektet PEID (Priority Environmental Infrastructure for Development) genomf&#xf6;rs av bolaget EPTISA vilka vann en internationell konkurrensupphandling. Projeket p&#xe5;b&#xf6;rjades 2016-09-01. Projektets m&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttning &#xe4;r att ge st&#xf6;d till milj&#xf6;ministeriet att ta fram anbudsunderlag som uppfyller EUs krav (JASPERS) f&#xf6;r vattenreningsverk och avfallsdeponier vilket kan finansieras med en mix av medel fr&#xe5;n serbiska staten, EU medel (IPA) och internationella finansiering institut. Projektet avslutas efter f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning i december 2022.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PEID project is implemented by the EPTISA Company which won an international bidding. The project aims to assist the Ministry of Environmental Protection to prepare tender documents fulfilling EU standards (JASPERS) for Waste Water Treatment Plants (WWTP) and Solid Waste Landfills for financing by a mix of national funding, EU Instrument Pre Accession (IPA)  and International Financing Institutions (IFI). The PEID project will provide technical to the Serbian Ministry of Environmental Protection as part of a process of capability and capacity development. The project has been extended and concludes end of 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
